<Page x:Class="Project_FREAK.Views.HelpPage"
      xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
      xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
      Background="#1E1E1E">
    <Grid Margin="32">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/>
            <RowDefinition Height="*"/>
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <DockPanel Grid.Row="0" Margin="0,0,0,20">
            <Button DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="Back to start" Padding="14,8" Click="BackToStartButton_Click"/>
            <StackPanel>
                <TextBlock Text="How to use Project FREAK" Foreground="White" FontSize="30" FontWeight="Bold"/>
                <TextBlock Text="Record a test, inspect its data, and configure the test stand." Foreground="#BDBDBD" FontSize="16" Margin="0,5,0,0"/>
            </StackPanel>
        </DockPanel>

        <ScrollViewer Grid.Row="1" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
            <StackPanel MaxWidth="1000" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                <Border Background="#292929" Padding="18" Margin="0,0,0,12" CornerRadius="6">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="Choose a task" Foreground="White" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="Record a Test opens the live sensor graphs and camera view. Review Recorded Data opens a saved test session. Settings is available here and from the menu at the top of the main window; Help is also available from that menu." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Background="#292929" Padding="18" Margin="0,0,0,12" CornerRadius="6">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="Record a test" Foreground="White" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="1. Before testing, check Settings for the LabJack connection status and confirm the sensor channels and calibration are correct. If Settings reports SIMULATION, the readings are simulated; do not use them as live hardware measurements or for hardware calibration." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="2. On the Record page, select Arm. The control changes to Disarm when armed. Only arm and start a motor test when the test stand is prepared and the area is clear, following your lab's approved procedure." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="3. Select Start. A five-second countdown runs before ignition and recording begin. Select Stop Recording to end the test; sensor data is saved automatically." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="4. Sessions are saved in a timestamped folder under Documents\\RocketTests. Video recording is included when the camera is available; a camera error does not prevent sensor data from recording." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Background="#292929" Padding="18" Margin="0,0,0,12" CornerRadius="6">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="Review a saved test" Foreground="White" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="1. Choose Open Data JSON and select a saved session's JSON file. The thrust and pressure graphs and session statistics will load. A matching video is opened automatically when its file is available; otherwise, choose Choose Video." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="2. Use Play/Pause and the slider to inspect the video. Drag the green START or red END line on either graph to select a time interval; the interval statistics update as you adjust it. The overall statistics continue to describe the full recording." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="3. Select Export .eng to export the thrust curve to the standard RASP / RockSim motor data format. A prompt will appear allowing you to adjust the burn interval and specify physical motor parameters." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Background="#292929" Padding="18" Margin="0,0,0,12" CornerRadius="6">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="Exporting to RASP / RockSim format (.eng)" Foreground="White" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="The RASP / .eng file format is the standard rocket motor data interchange format used by flight simulators such as OpenRocket, RockSim, and ThrustCurve.org." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="• Burn Interval: The exported thrust curve is normalized to begin at t = 0 with intermediate thrust values and ends with a 0 N point at burn completion. You can use your graph selection, full recording, or manually type start and end times in seconds." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="• Motor Parameters: Because the test stand only measures thrust, pressure, and time, the export dialog prompts you for the remaining physical parameters required by the RASP specification:" Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="    - Motor Name: Defaults to the calculated NAR/TRA designation (e.g. F32) from the interval's total impulse and average thrust, or enter a custom name." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="    - Casing Dimensions: Outer diameter and length in millimeters (mm)." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="    - Delays: Available ejection delay times separated by dashes (e.g. '4-8-12'), '0' for none, or 'P' for plugged (no ejection charge)." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="    - Propellant &amp; Total Mass: Mass of consumables and total loaded flight mass in kilograms (kg)." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="    - Manufacturer Code: Short identifier (e.g. MSP, AT, CTI, EST)." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="• Data Resolution: Choose standard resolution (up to 500 points — recommended for modern simulators), compact (100 points), classic RASP (max 32 points for vintage tools), or full recorded resolution. Peak thrust is automatically preserved." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>

                <Border Background="#292929" Padding="18" Margin="0,0,0,12" CornerRadius="6">
                    <StackPanel>
                        <TextBlock Text="Settings and setup" Foreground="White" FontSize="20" FontWeight="SemiBold" Margin="0,0,0,8"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="Apply uses changes for the current session; Save also stores them for future sessions. Settings includes hardware channels, sensor calibration, and the option to recalculate review data from raw sensor voltages. Calibration requires two different known loads and real sensor readings." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
                        <TextBlock Text="For a direct Ethernet connection to the test stand, Settings can configure the selected adapter to 192.168.20.2. Restore that adapter to DHCP when testing is finished. Changing network configuration may request administrator approval." Foreground="#D0D0D0" TextWrapping="Wrap"/>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>
            </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>
    </Grid>
</Page>